# Jarvis OS — Docker Compose stack environment (deploy/docker/.env).
#
# Compose reads `deploy/docker/.env` automatically. It is gitignored: NEVER
# commit real values. `make secrets` (also run by `make up`) creates it and
# appends a random value for every missing required secret below; it never
# overwrites a key that is already there. Everything else is optional.

# --- Required secrets (generated by `make secrets`) ---
# DJANGO_SECRET_KEY=
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# REDIS_PASSWORD=
# JARVIS_BFF_SHARED_SECRET=

# --- Optional overrides ---

# Deterministic fake LLM provider. Dev stack default: true (keeps `make
# test-e2e`/CI deterministic); daily stack (compose.daily.yml) default: false.
# AI_FAKE_PROVIDER=false

# Host directory bind-mounted into the worker as the Obsidian vault export
# target (default: the repo-local, gitignored .devdata/obsidian-vault).
# OBSIDIAN_VAULT_HOST_PATH=/absolute/path/to/your/vault

# Browser-facing origin of the daily stack's frontend (compose.daily.yml).
# APP_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3001

# Daily stack device pairing (Phase 4 branch 2). The header your reverse
# proxy sets to the browser's IP (Caddy: `header_up X-Real-IP
# {remote_host}` -> X-Real-IP); empty = no trusted proxy, PINs refused.
# TRUSTED_CLIENT_IP_HEADER=X-Real-IP
# Accept PINs even without a trusted client IP ("LAN gating off").
# DEVICE_PAIRING_ALLOW_UNKNOWN_IP=false

# Real providers for personal dogfooding (see the repo-root .env.example for
# what each one means).
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=
# NVIDIA_MODEL_ID=
# NVIDIA_BASE_URL=
# NVIDIA_EMBEDDING_MODEL_ID=
# NVIDIA_EMBEDDING_DIMENSION=1024
# OLLAMA_API_KEY=
# OLLAMA_MODEL_ID=
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
# OLLAMA_EMBED_MODEL_ID=
# OLLAMA_EMBED_DIMENSION=

# Real Telegram bot credentials (MVP 9 §4). Empty = the webhook rejects
# every request.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Google mail/calendar connector (Phase 5 branch 8; runbook
# docs/runbooks/google-connector.md). Client id/secret from the Desktop-app
# OAuth client; the refresh token is printed once by the host-side
# `manage.py connect_google` -- paste it here, then `make up`.
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# --- e2e run (`make test-e2e` against this stack) ---
# The Playwright smoke enrolls a device for the owner account (global
# setup runs `manage.py issue_pairing_code --plain` through E2E_MANAGE_CMD,
# e.g. "docker compose -f deploy/docker/compose.yml exec -T web uv run
# python manage.py") and drives the Telegram webhook with fixture
# credentials. Uncomment these for the e2e run only,
# then comment them out again (`make up` to apply either way): a publicly
# known webhook secret must never stay on the daily stack. The fixture
# values must match frontend/e2e/smoke.e2e.ts's defaults.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=e2e-fixture-bot-token
# TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=e2e-fixture-webhook-secret

# GitHub connector sidecar (Phase 5 branch 5, docs/mcp/github.md) --
# `docker compose --profile connectors up github-mcp`. The fine-grained PAT
# (registered repos only: contents:read, pull_requests:write, actions:read,
# metadata:read; 90-day expiry) is read ONLY by the `github-mcp` sidecar,
# never by web/worker. GITHUB_MCP_URL is what web/worker use to reach it.
# GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# GITHUB_MCP_URL=http://github-mcp:8080/mcp
